  "finalText": "I built the toggle micro-interaction as a 2 s comp on a light grey (#F2F2F7) background. The critic scores it 100/100 with no issues.\n\n- **Toggle track** (grey #D1D1D6 to green #34C759): the colour crossfades from 0.4 s to 0.7 s, starting with the knob.\n- **Toggle knob** (white, 90 px): slides from the left to the right end from 0.4 s, with a small overshoot about 4 px past the end and settling by 0.95 s. It stretches to 112×91 mid-travel and squashes to 95×105 on arrival before returning to round by 1.02 s.\n- **Toggle check** (green stroke): draws on from 0.8 s over 0.25 s once the knob has nearly settled, and follows the knob's position.\n\nThe first frame is the off state and the on state holds from about 1.0 s to the end. The comp is still 2 s, so you could shorten it to about 1.4 s if you want a tighter loop-ready clip. I can also make the travel snappier with a spring, or add a faint knob shadow."
